            "id": "6d55e3d6-e3c6-aa93-338d-a91b6dc06133",
            "experimentationGroup": "cstprodmsit~aletheia",
            "displayName": "Compact CLI system prompt",
            "description": "Run an A/B test in Copilot CLI to evaluate a compact system prompt that removes repeated guidance now duplicated across system sections, model-specific tuning, tool descriptions and schemas, and SQL/skill instructions. The current prompt adds about 2,000-2,400 static tokens per request depending on model. Treatment enables copilot_cli_compact_system_prompt and uses compact versions of those prompt components; control keeps the current prompt and must remain byte-identical when the experiment is off. Target is CLI request flows across models. Goal is to preserve key behavioral constraints and maintain comparable success rate while reducing static/input tokens and ideally lowering cost. Monitor success rate, mean/median and cache-optimal cost, static/input/output tokens, LLM roundtrips, tool calls, parallel tool-call rate, and model-specific regressions. Risks: mixed offline cost/trajectory signals despite prompt-size reduction; no LLM capacity impact expected.",
